\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Results on 48-taxon dataset.} (a)-(b) We show the average RF rates with standard errors over 20 replicates for the methods ASTRAL, wQFM (wQFM-uncorrected), and wQFM+QT-WEAVER (wQFM-corrected). (a) The amount of ILS was varied from high to low, keeping the number of genes fixed at 1000 and sequence length at 500bp. (b) The number of genes was varied keeping ILS fixed at moderate (1X) and the sequence length at 500bp. (c)-(d) Average Jensen-Shannon divergence of the quartet distributions before and after correction with respect to the true quartet distributions. }}{13}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
